  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Russia Education Aid for Development (READ) Trust Fund</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&quot;The development objective of the READ TF is to generate and disseminate  operational knowledge to strengthen the effectiveness and performance  of the systems and institutions in low-income countries that are  responsible for measuring and/or using learning outcomes to improve  teaching and learning. This objective will be realized through a  two-pronged program design, supporting country-level and global-level  activities and outcomes. The TF will support analytical work to  (a)strengthen existing/help establish new systems/institutions that  formulate learning goals, (b) measure learning outcomes through  student assessments, (c) use learning outcome measures to improve  teaching/instruction. The TF will focus on FTI countries that are also  Russia aid priority countries.
 For countries explicitly identified for support, the main benefits will  be the establishment or strengthening of a unit(s)in education  ministries to manage learning assessments and use their results to  improve teaching and learning and make the needed operational/policy  improvements to raise learning outcomes, which in turn will help  prospects for social/economic progress. Other countries will also  benefit from &quot;&quot;global&quot;&quot; knowledge generation and sharing activities  (training, workshops, materials).
      READ TF would complement existing external funding sources  available to FTI countries&apos; education sectors, by being a source that  is singularly dedicated to improving learning outcomes through student  assessments.&quot;</narrative>
  </description>
